## Summary
The tracking leftovers from `docs/gaps.md` U1/U3/U4/U9 are still missing:
- the temporary tracking point TT and the TK (tracking) point modifier;
- PolarSnap (SNAPTYPE 1, POLARDIST);
- polar angles relative to the last segment (POLARMODE bit 2);
- additional polar angles (POLARADDANG);
- Extension from ellipse and spline ends;
- Temporary track point in the snap menu;
- the tracking options in Drafting Settings.

## Scope
- TT at any point prompt and in the Shift+right-click snap menu: acquire a temporary tracking point, then track from it.
- TK modifier: a sequence of tracking points; Enter ends it and the point is used.
- PolarSnap: snap along polar tracking paths at POLARDIST increments.
- POLARMODE bits for relative-to-last-segment and for tracking on all polar angles vs orthogonal only.
- POLARADDANG / additional angles.
- Extension snap on elliptical arcs and open splines.
- The matching Drafting Settings controls, kept thin.
- Command-line forms and system variables, so all of it is reachable headless.

## Expected
Tracking behaves like publicly documented AutoCAD polar and object snap tracking.

## Summary
Annotative scaling does nothing (`docs/gaps.md` F12). The annotative flag is stored, but nothing scales. There's no annotation scale list and no "Annotative Object Scale" commands; four menu items are uncovered.

## Scope
- Annotation scales:
  - the CANNOSCALE variable;
  - the drawing's scale list (SCALELISTEDIT: add, delete, reset to the default metric or imperial list);
  - each viewport's annotation scale, following the viewport scale by default.
- Annotative text, MText, dimensions, leaders/multileaders, hatches and blocks/attributes:
  - each object holds the set of scales it supports;
  - an object draws at paper height × the scale of the current model view or viewport;
  - an object is shown only in views whose scale it supports, unless ANNOALLVISIBLE is 1;
  - ANNOAUTOSCALE adds the current scale to all annotative objects when the scale changes.
- Commands:
  - OBJECTSCALE (Add/Delete a scale on selected objects), with the menu items Annotative Object Scale > Add/Delete, Add Current Scale and Remove Current Scale;
  - ANNORESET;
  - ANNOUPDATE.
- DXF: annotative flags and scale contexts as far as the public DXF Reference documents them (AcDbContextDataManager / ACDB_ANNOTATIONSCALES dictionary, the scale list in the ACAD_SCALELIST dictionary). Where they are undocumented, use our own xdata and list it under Limits.
- Status bar: the annotation scale list (thin UI).
- JSON forms; programmatic calls never open dialogs.

## Expected
Annotative objects keep the same paper size in every viewport scale, like publicly documented AutoCAD annotative scaling.

