## Summary
Right-click menus cover only a few places (`docs/gaps.md` U7). The canvas has a basic context menu (`crates/ui-egui/src/context_menu.rs`), but:
- the menu doesn't change while a command runs;
- selected objects get no menu specific to their type;
- the command line, palettes and drawing tabs have no menus.

## Scope
- **Canvas, while a command runs:**
  - Enter, Cancel and Recent Input;
  - the current prompt's keywords as menu items;
  - Snap Overrides submenu, Pan/Zoom.
  - Each item sends the same input as typing it.
- **Canvas with a selection:**
  - Repeat last command;
  - Cut/Copy/Copy with Base Point/Paste;
  - Erase/Move/Copy Selection/Scale/Rotate, Draw Order;
  - Group/Ungroup when those commands exist;
  - Isolate when it exists;
  - Select Similar, Deselect All;
  - Quick Select, Properties;
  - object-specific items (Edit Text for text, Block Editor/Edit Attributes for blocks, Hatch Edit, Polyline Edit…).
- **Canvas, no selection:** Repeat/Recent commands, Paste, Pan/Zoom, Quick Select, Options.
- **Command line:** Recent Commands, Copy History, Input Settings, Clear.
- **Drawing tabs:** New/Open/Save/Save All/Close/Close All Others; **layout tabs:** New Layout, From Template, Delete, Rename, Move or Copy, Select All Layouts, Page Setup, Plot.
- **Palettes (Properties, Layers):** relevant menus where they are missing.
- All items go through `app.run` / `app.start` / `app.cmdline` (thin UI); items for missing commands are left out, not stubbed.

## Expected
Right-click works in all the places a user would expect, like publicly documented AutoCAD shortcut menus.

## Summary
"Saving drops whatever we don't model" (`docs/gaps.md` Top-10 #1 and FF1, an alpha blocker) has been partly fixed by #201, #204, #208, #209, #213, #223, #147 and #162. Open PRs add MULTILEADER (#459), groups (#417), VIEW/VPORT tables (#463) and SORTENTSTABLE (#439). The row no longer says what is still lost.

## Scope
- Audit, with synthetic DXF files built from the public DXF Reference, what survives open → save → reopen on current main, for:
  - unknown entities in model space, paper space and blocks;
  - unknown objects in the named object dictionary and nested dictionaries;
  - foreign xdata (other APPIDs) on entities, tables and blocks;
  - extension dictionaries (102 {ACAD_XDICTIONARY) on entities and table records;
  - IMAGE + IMAGEDEF + IMAGEDEF_REACTOR;
  - UCS table, layer states, block descriptions;
  - true colours and colour books on every object type;
  - transparency;
  - hyperlinks (xdata PE_URL);
  - DICTIONARYVAR, XRECORDs, persistent reactors.
- Fix what is still lost, keeping data as raw groups where we don't model it, with handles remapped consistently. Owner/reactor handles must point at real objects after save.
- Do the same through the DWG bridge where the bridge allows it, and list acadrust gaps.
- Update the Top-10 #1 and FF1 rows to the true state.

## Expected
Opening a colleague's file and saving it keeps everything CADCraft doesn't edit.

## Summary
TABLE objects are basic (`docs/gaps.md` F11). There are:
- no cell styles (title, header and data, plus custom ones);
- no formulas;
- no table breaking;
- no data links.

## Scope
- **Cell styles in TABLESTYLE:** text style, height, colour, fill, alignment, margins, borders, data format, rows per cell style. Covered in the model, the TABLESTYLE command (JSON and typed), rendering, and DXF (TABLESTYLE / CELLSTYLEMAP as far as the public DXF Reference documents them; otherwise our own xdata, listed under Limits).
- **Formulas in cells:**
  - `=Sum(A1:B3)`, Average, Count, cell references and arithmetic;
  - evaluated with a bounded parser (no recursion blow-up; circular references show an error);
  - stored as the formula, with the evaluated text shown;
  - recalculated on edit, UPDATEFIELD and REGEN;
  - TABLEDIT / table.set cell formula, plus insert-formula options.
- **Table breaking:** the TABLEBREAK property (direction, repeat top/bottom labels, manual heights, spacing); the table is drawn in several parts; grips move the parts.
- **Data links** (DATALINK to a CSV file, update from the source): in scope only if cheap and safe (file read through the host, never from JSON without a path), otherwise listed under Limits.
- **Table export:** TABLEEXPORT to CSV.
- JSON forms for everything; programmatic calls never open dialogs.

## Expected
Tables can be styled, can calculate, and can be broken across a sheet like publicly documented AutoCAD tables.

## Summary
CADCraft can't use a user's own support files (`docs/gaps.md` FF9):
- no drawing templates (DWT);
- no user linetype (`.lin`) or hatch pattern (`.pat`) files;
- no command alias file (`.pgp`).

`.ctb`/`.stb` and `.pc3` are covered elsewhere (#410 / plotters).

## Scope
- **LINETYPE Load / -LINETYPE Load from a user `.lin` file:**
  - simple and complex lines, with text `["TEXT",STYLE,S=…,R=…,X=…,Y=…]` and shape references (shapes need SHX, so they are skipped with a note);
  - the parser follows the publicly documented LIN syntax.
- **HATCH from a user `.pat` file:**
  - the pattern list gains the file's patterns, using the publicly documented PAT syntax;
  - patterns are kept in the drawing, round-trip through DXF as today's custom patterns (#290), and are capped in line families and dash counts.
- **Templates:**
  - NEW / QNEW from a `.dwt` (read as DWG), or from a `.dxf` template;
  - a default template setting (OPTIONS from #23, or a system variable if that isn't merged);
  - SAVEAS to `.dwt` (DWG content, our writer).
- **ALIASEDIT/REINIT:** load a user `.pgp`-style alias file (`ALIAS, *COMMAND` lines, publicly documented format) that adds or overrides command aliases; we ship no `.pgp`.
- **Files and safety:**
  - every file comes from the user (path or picker); nothing from Autodesk is bundled or copied;
  - file reads go through the host (no fs in wasm);
  - hostile input never panics.
- JSON forms; programmatic calls never open dialogs.

## Expected
Users can bring their own templates, linetypes, hatch patterns and aliases.

## Summary
These prompt options still print "not available yet" (`docs/gaps.md` F1, an alpha blocker; #408 and #397 did the rest):
- PEDIT Edit vertex: Break, Regen and Tangent;
- some SPLINEDIT options.

Closed splines also keep a fit tolerance but ignore it.

## Scope
- **PEDIT Edit vertex** (the vertex marker loop: Next, Previous, Break, Insert, Move, Regen, Straighten, Tangent, Width, eXit):
  - Break: from the marked vertex to a second chosen vertex (Go), splitting the polyline;
  - Regen;
  - Tangent: store the tangent direction used by Fit;
  - check Insert/Move/Straighten/Width as well.
- **SPLINEDIT:** go through all options and implement every one that says "not available yet":
  - Close/Open, Join, Fit data (Add/Close/Delete/Kink/Move/Purge/Tangents/toLerance/eXit);
  - Edit vertex (Add/Delete/Elevate order/Move/Weight);
  - convert to Polyline, Reverse, Undo.
- **Closed splines:** honour the fit tolerance (least-squares approximation on periodic splines, the counterpart of #408's open-spline approximation).
- Typed prompts and JSON forms; tests per option.

## Expected
No "not available yet" left in PEDIT and SPLINEDIT.

## Summary
The inquiry tools are thin (`docs/gaps.md` F22):
- COUNT counts block inserts in model space only;
- CAL is only an evaluator, and there is no QuickCalc palette;
- there is no drawing comparison (COMPARE).

MASSPROP is handled separately by #510 (#526) for regions.

## Scope
- **COUNT:**
  - counts inserts of a block in model space, paper space layouts and nested inside other blocks (with multiplication), or in a selection;
  - optional same-geometry counting of non-block objects (COUNT "objects like this one", where cheap);
  - COUNTLIST / the JSON form returns per-block counts;
  - highlight counted objects;
  - COUNTFIELD-like insertion of the count as a table if cheap.
- **QuickCalc palette (QUICKCALC, QC):**
  - expression input with history;
  - units conversion (length, area, volume, angle) and variables;
  - "Get coordinates/distance/angle/intersection" picks from the drawing via the command system;
